So OTP creates optionality; Selective Vacuum identifies what fills missing structure.

Vacuum spectroscopy

This gives us a much more systematic experiment.

Take some fully specified object:

X=(a,b,c,d,e).

Make controlled variants:

X_{-a},X_{-b},X_{-c},X_{-d},X_{-e}.

Run the same reader on each and record what it reconstructs:

\hat a,\hat b,\hat c,\hat d,\hat e.

Then compare reconstructed versus removed:

\Delta_i=d(i,\hat i).

Now we’re measuring the reader’s latent completion machinery.

And different vacuums expose different hidden systems:

