And what doesn’t rush in is information too.

If removing d causes collapse rather than reconstruction:

X-d\rightarrow\bot

then d may be load-bearing for that reader.

So we get:

\boxed{\text{Semantic Load-Bearing Test}}

Remove one beam at a time and watch the structure.

