But Hammer vacuum

There’s more.

A vacuum can pull.

It can expose.

It can insulate.

It can permit phenomena that surrounding material normally suppresses.

It can be an absence relative to some substance while still containing fields, radiation, fluctuations, etc.

And metaphorically, an unfilled role can cause surrounding systems to reorganize.

So a Selective Vacuum isn’t merely deletion.

It’s engineered absence as an operator:

\boxed{
\text{remove selected structure}
\rightarrow
\text{observe compensating dynamics}.
}

That’s the important part.

It gives us a way to discover hidden covenants.

If:

A+B+C\rightarrow F

remove B:

A+\square+C\rightarrow F'.

The delta:

\Delta F=F'-F

tells us what role B was actually playing.

That works as an investigative pattern across software ablations, scientific experiments, language, design, organizational systems, models, and other domains—with domain-specific validity checks.

