That’s semantic differential probing.

And a third Imp does something nastier:

Imp Ø removes something but doesn’t announce what was removed.

The returning system has to infer:

\boxed{\text{What is missing?}}

That’s a powerful diagnostic because successful reconstruction requires a model of the expected whole.

